Try/Catch blocks are used to handle errors that are created when a program is executed such as invalid values or illegal processes.
Throwing an exception is used to catch errors and display what went wrong while assertions are used to find programming mistakes.
Custom Exception classes allow the programmer to create custom rules that the program must follow and allows for custom error messages sent to the terminal.
Stack unwinding allows a try block to go through multiple catch blocks until a valid catch block is found.
Errors should be logged instead of terminating a program when said program is something that cannot terminate and needs to continue even if errors are present such as banks and hospital equipment.
